                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "44109643",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198066590240",
                            "num_reviews": 3404,
                            "playtime_forever": 40,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 40,
                            "last_played": 1727922421
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Yeah, I can't recommend this game now in 2024 (almost 2025). This was released in 2017 and we were more forgiving of VR games back then. Thankfully, we have higher standards now. This is a repetitive puzzle game. You have the same exact puzzle over and over and over again. I got pretty far into the game and it was always just a matter of using power-ups to slow the game down so you can fit the shape into the hole in the wall.\n\nThere's just not enough visual variety and there's also not enough gameplay variety. You start from scratch every time you lose as well so the only reason to keep playing is for the leaderboard. Tetris Connected makes this game look out-dated and puts it to shame. If you notice a lot of the positive reviews have less than 2 hours. This game is fun for about 30 minutes. You have 30 minutes of fun. Then you realize this is just dumb. \n\nAlso, you're using an Xbox one controller if you want the controls to work correctly on the Meta Quest 3. Trust me, you'll want to use a gamepad for this game. The problem is that it's just not worth it.",
